-- title:
--   The finite-evidence history topology over $\mathbb Z^d$
-- statement:
--   A basic neighborhood of a history $H$ is built recursively: include $H$; for each included history $\Gamma$ choose a finite set $F_\Gamma\subseteq\mathrm{end}(\Gamma)$ and include every one-step extension $\Gamma^\frown M$ with $M\in\mathcal X$ and $F_\Gamma\subseteq M\subsetneq\mathrm{end}(\Gamma)$. The **finite-evidence history topology** is generated by all basic neighborhoods of all histories. $\mathcal H_K$ denotes the histories beginning at $K$.
--
--   The paper notes (p.57) that this topology does not depend on the dimension; this module is the published `LocalBreadth.historyTopology` over an arbitrary universe.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The finite sets form a total rule $f$ on histories (values on histories never included are unused). The topology is a `def`, used as `IsOpen[historyTopologyP X]`.
-- source:
--   Kleinberg, Wei, Characterizing Local Breadth in Language Generation, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 f924cbfc309339291b1a61b8504342f4050ece6e4e903dd18b2bf541446f1064), Definition 5.3, p.25; §7.3.1, p.57

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LocalBreadth_Supplement_HistoryP

namespace LocalBreadth.Supplement

variable {P : Type} (X : Set (Set P))

/-- A finite-test rule (Definition 5.3): one finite set `F_Γ ⊆ end(Γ)` for each history `Γ`.

**Formalization Note.** The rule is total; its values on histories that are not included are unused. -/
def IsTestRuleP (f : HistoryP P X → Finset P) : Prop := ∀ Γ, (f Γ : Set P) ⊆ Γ.last

/-- The histories included when the recursion of Definition 5.3 starts at `H`, under the rule `f`:
start with `H`, and from an included `Γ` include every `Γ⌢M` with `F_Γ ⊆ M ⊊ end(Γ)`, `M ∈ X`. -/
inductive ReachP (f : HistoryP P X → Finset P) (H : HistoryP P X) : HistoryP P X → Prop
  | base : ReachP f H H
  | step {Γ : HistoryP P X} (hΓ : ReachP f H Γ) (M : Set P) (hM : M ∈ X) (hlt : M ⊂ Γ.last)
      (hF : (f Γ : Set P) ⊆ M) : ReachP f H (Γ.snoc M hM hlt)

/-- A **basic neighborhood** of `H`, Definition 5.3, p.25. -/
def basicNhdP (H : HistoryP P X) (f : HistoryP P X → Finset P) : Set (HistoryP P X) :=
  {Γ | ReachP X f H Γ}

/-- All basic neighborhoods, for all starting histories and all choices of finite sets. -/
def basicSetsP : Set (Set (HistoryP P X)) :=
  {U | ∃ (H : HistoryP P X) (f : HistoryP P X → Finset P), IsTestRuleP X f ∧ U = basicNhdP X H f}

/-- The **finite-evidence history topology** over a universe `P`. Kleinberg, Wei, STOC 2027
submission (manuscript sha256 f924cbfc…), Definition 5.3, p.25, used in §7 (p.57): the topology
generated by the basic neighborhoods.

**Formalization Note.** The published `LocalBreadth.historyTopology` with `ℤ` replaced by `P`. A `def`,
used through `IsOpen[historyTopologyP X]`, rather than an instance. -/
@[instance_reducible] def historyTopologyP : TopologicalSpace (HistoryP P X) :=
  TopologicalSpace.generateFrom (basicSetsP X)

/-- `ℋ_K`, the histories beginning at `K` (p.57). -/
def historiesFromP (K : Set P) : Set (HistoryP P X) := {H | H.first = K}

end LocalBreadth.Supplement


